Z||000000||William Federle||10-05-2000||01:27 PM||||I just had to replace my alternator belt for<BR>the second time in slightly less than 1 year.<BR>I think that my problem has something to do with the fact that I'm using a toothed vbelt<BR>instead of a solid vbelt. <P>Has anyone been able to find a place that sells a solid vbelt for a Fiero? I tried<BR>NAPA, Autozone, and Advance Auto and none of<BR>them have a solid belt for the Fiero.<P>Was the original belt (1984 SE) a toothed<BR>belt?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||10-05-2000||02:13 PM||||I just went through the same thing. Toothed belts are for geared pulleys and ribbed belts are a way to charge more for less rubber. The last one I bought stretched so much I couldn't adjust any more. I went to the dealer and got a solid belt for half the cost as the crappy ribbed one. I chose a belt that was half an inch shorter in length than the original. It was a bit harder to get on but gives me a little more room to stretch. No more slipping.||||reg||1
